                        ],
                        "form": "das Chrisam"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f4adf256-83fc-394b-803d-f04c440ec23d",
                        "entry_id": "23b556cb-81c9-3afa-8df3-1b7bfb5e8c5b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "wertvolles gesegnetes Öl für Salbungen, das unter anderem bei der Firmung, Taufe und der Priesterweihe benutzt wird"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Katholische Kirche",
                            "Orthodoxe Kirche"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2dd8593-fee4-4570-93d8-55bd16a781fa",
                                "sense_id": "f4adf256-83fc-394b-803d-f04c440ec23d",
                                "text": "„Bei der Feier der Taufe erfolgt unmittelbar im Anschluss an den eigentlichen Taufakt die Salbung mit Chrisam.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c247db03-da49-468f-bde3-9821f753716f",
                                "sense_id": "f4adf256-83fc-394b-803d-f04c440ec23d",
                                "text": "„Gemäß Ordo Romanus XI, somit im Frühmittelalter, dürfen die Gläubigen noch mit Chrisam vermischtes Taufwasser mit nach Hause nehmen.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f084a56-880f-4d8d-bef3-cc69ff6c759b",
                                "sense_id": "f4adf256-83fc-394b-803d-f04c440ec23d",
                                "text": "„Die erforderliche Handlung besteht in einer Salbung mit Chrisam unter Auflegung der Hand zusammen mit einer gültigen Formel.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53015fcc-9819-46d1-b09f-bcd105be4379",
                                "sense_id": "f4adf256-83fc-394b-803d-f04c440ec23d",
                                "text": "„Allein die Bischöfe aber sollen die 831 Getauften an der Stirn mit dem Chrisam bezeichnen, da die Salbung mit diesem nur von Bischöfen gespendet werden darf.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab7ff713-d590-4234-9a19-d4cf26776891",
                                "sense_id": "f4adf256-83fc-394b-803d-f04c440ec23d",
                                "text": "„Viel weniger Aufmerksamkeit widmete man der Salbung mit Chrisam, die ein Zeichen besonderer Berufung ist, wie etwa im Alten Testament der Propheten und Könige.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1a2c8dc8-030e-4e30-816b-a2e84723d436",
                        "source_entry_id": "23b556cb-81c9-3afa-8df3-1b7bfb5e8c5b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f4adf256-83fc-394b-803d-f04c440ec23d",
                        "source_sense_description": "Christentum: wertvolles gesegnetes Öl für Salbungen",
                        "target_lang_word": "chrism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chrism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                        "entry_id": "b03112ad-dc6d-302d-8ddb-83ce7a0df7e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mixture of oil and balm, consecrated for use as an anointing fluid in certain Christian ceremonies, especially confirmation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd2e5c6d-4bf2-4749-a557-b96bef779379",
                                                "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                                "text": "A reinforcement of fresh troops staggered in, one man soaked and dripping, his hair sticky with the chrism of poured beer, another with his pockets crammed with sauce-bottles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75e1f4c4-b153-40d5-849f-70058f87e342",
                                                "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                                "text": "I observe no confirmation of this reversal and Pole specifically restored chrisms in 1555 (Cardwell, op. cit. i. 147)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f7af796-f291-4ab2-8561-8491f065f41f",
                                                "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                                "text": "‘The King,’ Will cried, ‘is my master and bathed in the chrism of the Lord God.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f32f1cc6-7573-492b-8381-05d137b283af",
                                                "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                                "text": "For Christian examples of condensed symbols, consider the sacraments, particularly the Eucharist and the Chrisms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e524d0e-4956-4548-b842-7fbcee9a3c28",
                                                "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                                "text": "He was more dangerous than the plump satisfied ones, he was so sure of the value of his witchcraft, the holy oils and chrisms and unctions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72cd444b-fce5-42b6-bad1-dbc6e3eff7de",
                                                "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                                "text": "Miraculously moist, the chrism was kept in an ampulla in Reims cathedral where the coronations of the kings of France were held."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "166f8c92-1629-45aa-a877-9d6265153f34",
                                                "sense_id": "6a54f609-9564-38d2-87d0-3c7a26ceb4a2",
                                                "text": "[…]even if modest gestures of modernisation have slimmed down the ceremony, the chrism of unction is no longer perfumed with animal effluents—ambergris, musk and civet—and Andrew Lloyd Webber added to Handel and Elgar?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
